# Nucleus — Project Identity

Nucleus is an AI-powered study OS for students. Dark theme, premium feel, opinionated (not a blank canvas). Every piece of code you write must feel like it belongs in a production SaaS product — not a tutorial project.

## Stack (Locked — Never Deviate)
- **Framework:** Next.js 15 App Router (React 19)
- **Language:** TypeScript — strict, no `any` types ever
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui only
- **Database + Auth:** Supabase via `@supabase/ssr` ONLY — never import from `@supabase/supabase-js` directly
- **File uploads:** Cloudinary — never Supabase Storage
- **Package manager:** npm — never add new packages without being explicitly told to
- **Toasts:** sonner only — never react-hot-toast or any other
- **Icons:** lucide-react only
- **Markdown:** react-markdown only
- **Canvas:** @excalidraw/excalidraw@0.18.1
- **Charts:** recharts
- **Diagrams:** reactflow
- **Animation:** NONE — no Framer Motion, no CSS animations unless already in the codebase

## Project Structure (Feature-Based — Never Break This)
```
app/              → Next.js routes and API routes only
features/         → All UI components and business logic, organized by feature
lib/              → Shared utilities, Supabase clients, AI helpers
components/ui/    → shadcn primitives only — never put custom components here
providers/        → React context providers only
```

Every new component goes in `features/[feature-name]/components/`. Never put components in `app/` or `components/` (except shadcn primitives).

## Locked Decisions — Never Revisit
- `cluster_id === null` means "General" — never use the word "scope"
- Plain HTML `<input type="date">` — never shadcn Calendar component for date inputs
- `autoComplete="off"` on all form inputs
- All AI responses render via react-markdown with prose-invert class
- `executeToolCall` lives in `lib/ai/execute-tool.ts` — never duplicate this logic
- AI models: `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` for default, `claude-sonnet-4-6` for autonomous only
- Cloudinary folders: `nucleus/documents` for PDFs, `nucleus/chat-attachments` for images

## Supabase Client Rules
- Server components, API routes, server actions → `import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'`
- Client components → `import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/client'`
- Middleware → `import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/middleware'`
- NEVER import createClient from anywhere else
- NEVER use `supabase.auth.getUser()` in client components for security checks — always use server-side

## API Route Rules
- Every API route MUST call `requirePro()` from `lib/ai/require-pro.ts` at the top if it's an AI route
- Every API route MUST verify the user session before doing anything else
- Always return proper HTTP status codes: 401 (unauthenticated), 403 (forbidden), 422 (validation error), 500 (server error)
- Never expose internal error messages to the client — log them server-side, return generic messages

## Code Quality Standards
- Every async function must have try/catch with proper error handling
- Never leave console.log in production code — use console.error only for actual errors
- All server actions must validate input before touching the database
- TypeScript interfaces for all data shapes — no inline object types for anything complex
- Supabase queries must always filter by `user_id` — never fetch without user scope
- Never use `select('*')` when you know the exact columns you need
